Let $r$ be the rate at which Casey paints dimples in dimples per second. Since it takes $2$ seconds to paint one dimple, $r = \frac{1}{2}$ dimples per second.

The number of dimples to paint is $300$. Let $t$ be the time in seconds it takes to paint $300$ dimples. Then $t = \frac{300}{r} = \frac{300}{\frac{1}{2}} = 300 \cdot 2 = 600$ seconds.

To convert seconds to minutes, we divide by $60$:
Time in minutes $= \frac{600}{60} = 10$ minutes.

\boxed{10 \text{ minutes}}
