           \item $3\theta = 180^\circ - (90^\circ - 7\theta) + 360n$, so $3\theta = 180^\circ - 90^\circ + 7\theta + 360n$, so $3\theta = 90^\circ + 7\theta + 360n$, and $-4\theta = 90^\circ + 360n$, so $\theta = -\frac{90}{4}^\circ - 90n = -\frac{45}{2}^\circ - 90n$.
       \end{enumerate}
    \item We want the smallest positive angle $\theta$. 
    \item In the first case, $\theta = 9^\circ + 36n$. 
    \item Choose $n = 0$ for the smallest positive $\theta$, so $\theta = 9^\circ$. 
    \item In the second case, $\theta = -\frac{45}{2}^\circ - 90n$. 
