Let the side length of the cube be $s$. The volume of the cube is given by $V = s^3$. We are given that $V = 0.027$ cubic meters.
So, $s^3 = 0.027$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s = \sqrt[3]{0.027} = 0.3$ meters.
The surface area of one face of the cube is $s^2 = (0.3)^2 = 0.09$ square meters.
Since a cube has six faces, the total surface area of the cube is $6s^2 = 6(0.09) = 0.54$ square meters.
\end{aligned}
}
